{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Hunting of a beast.</b> To include every kosher beast." "<b>Or bird.</b> Whether many or few. From here they said: if he slaughtered a hundred animals in one place, one covering suffices for all of them; if he slaughtered a beast and a bird in one place, one covering suffices for all of them." "<b>Beast or bird.</b> A bird is likened to a beast: just as a beast is not offered on the altar, so too a bird that is not offered — excluding a bird that is offered on the altar, whose blood does not require covering." "<b>And shall cover it with dust.</b> So that it is not fit for eating."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:07.631769248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}